   "tuning": [],
   "is_new": true,
   "source": {
    "label": "lem:local_more_explicit_lower_bound",
    "number": "Corollary 1",
    "quote": "Then, we have $T^{\\star}_{\\ell}\\left(\\boldsymbol{\\nu} ; \\epsilon\\right) \\geq \\max\\left\\{ T^{\\star}_{\\mathrm{KL}}(\\boldsymbol{\\nu}) , c(\\epsilon)^{-1} T^{\\star}_{\\mathrm{TV}^2}\\left(\\boldsymbol{\\nu}\\right)  \\right\\}$ ... Then, we have $T^{\\star}_{\\mathrm{TV}^2}\\left(\\boldsymbol{\\nu}\\right)\\ge 2 T^{\\star}_{\\mathrm{KL}}(\\boldsymbol{\\nu})$ and $T^{\\star}_{\\mathrm{TV}^2}\\left(\\boldsymbol{\\nu}\\right) =  T^{\\star}_{\\mathrm{KL}}(\\boldsymbol{\\nu}_{\\mathrm{G}})/2$."
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Combined Corollary 1 with Theorem 3 to state a bound on E[tau]. For Bernoulli instances T_TV2 = T_KL(nu_G)/2 where nu_G is unit-variance Gaussian with same means."
